  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 2 medium food storage containers and 2 resealable plastic bags.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, pat chicken dry with paper towels and cut crosswise into thin strips. Season with spices.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "227 g chicken breasts, boneless skinless\n¼ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp black pepper\n⅛ tsp garlic powder"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add chicken and cook, stirring occasionally, until cooked through, 4-5 minutes. Remove from heat, add barbecue sauce, and stir to coat. Set aside to cool, 10 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n2 tbsp barbecue sauce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, divide chips between resealable plastic bags and set aside. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "3 cups potato chips, wavy cut"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place shredded cabbage and dressing in a medium bowl, then stir to combine the slaw. \n\n\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 ½ cups shredded cabbage (coleslaw mix)\n2 tbsp coleslaw dressing"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the chicken is cool, place tortillas on a flat surface, then divide barbecue chicken, slaw, and cheese between them. Roll tightly to close and, using a clean cutting board, cut in half. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "⅔ cup cheddar cheese, shredded"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Divide wraps between storage containers, cover, and refrigerate until ready to eat. Enjoy wraps with potato chips!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
